---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../../../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Reading a foundation repair bid: pier count, methods, and red flags"
  description="How to read a foundation repair proposal in Arizona — pier count, methods, language, and common red flags."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Reading a foundation repair bid</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A foundation repair bid is a sales document as much as a technical one. Look at three things carefully.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Pier count</h2>
      <p>
        More is not automatically better. Ask why that exact number and spacing was chosen and what the floor data showed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Method</h2>
      <p>
        Helical piers, push piers, and other systems behave differently in expansive clay. Make sure the recommendation matches the direction of movement (settlement vs heave).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Language</h2>
      <p>
        Watch for urgency, worst-case framing, and vague warranty language. Clear scope, clear exclusions, and a willingness to discuss monitoring are better signs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Red flags</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Pressure to sign the same day</li>
        <li>Refusal to share the actual elevation data</li>
        <li>Recommendations that ignore obvious drainage problems</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="contact-box">
        <p><strong>Have a bid you want a second set of eyes on?</strong></p>
        <a class="phone-link" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>{PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
